+---
+id: dl-001-use-strict-rfc-6901-pointer-evaluation
+type: decision-log
+title: "Use strict RFC 6901 pointer evaluation"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Services need one interoperable way to resolve values in JSON documents, and later features will build
+on this primitive.
+
+## Decision
+
+Evaluate pointers strictly according to RFC 6901: every non-root pointer begins with `/`, only `~0` and
+`~1` are valid token escapes, and array indices are `0` or non-zero decimal digits without leading zeroes.
+The array append token (`-`) and paths that do not identify a concrete value raise an error.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Callers receive a value only for an unambiguous, existing location. Invalid input and missing locations
+cannot be silently confused with JSON values such as `false` or `null`.
